# Convex documentation

Use the official Convex docs as the source of truth: [https://docs.convex.dev/home](https://docs.convex.dev/home)

When implementing or changing Convex code, fetch the relevant page as markdown rather than relying on memory.

- Page markdown: `https://docs.convex.dev/<path>.md` (or request `Accept: text/markdown`)
- Docs index: [https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt](https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt)
- Platform overview: [https://www.convex.dev/llms.txt](https://www.convex.dev/llms.txt)

This repo’s app is Next.js (`flashycardy`). Start with:

- [Next.js Quickstart](https://docs.convex.dev/quickstart/nextjs.md)
- [Next.js App Router](https://docs.convex.dev/client/nextjs/app-router.md)
- [Functions](https://docs.convex.dev/functions/overview.md)
- [Queries](https://docs.convex.dev/functions/query-functions.md)
- [Mutations](https://docs.convex.dev/functions/mutation-functions.md)
- [Database](https://docs.convex.dev/database/overview.md)
- [Schemas](https://docs.convex.dev/database/schemas.md)
- [Authentication](https://docs.convex.dev/auth/overview.md)
- [Best Practices](https://docs.convex.dev/understanding/best-practices.md)
- [The Zen of Convex](https://docs.convex.dev/understanding/zen.md)

Follow `.cursor/rules/convex_rules.mdc` for function syntax, validators, schema, queries, mutations, actions, scheduling, and file storage.
